{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>First passage</b><br>גל [stream/spring]. Like גלות עליות [streams of the upper pools], close in meaning to מעין." "<b>Second passage</b><br>Now you are considered like גן נעול [a locked garden], into which no person may enter, and as though you planted a pomegranate orchard with fruit, every delicacy mixed with every kind of spice, and the meaning is that every pleasant and good fragrance is joined in you, and you are like מעין גנים באר מים חיים [a spring of gardens, a well of living waters] that restore a weary soul." "<b>Third passage</b><br>גל נעול [a locked spring]. [The daughters of Israel], the modest ones."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:44:20.153873754Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}